  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\alpha, \\beta$ be roots of $x^2+\\sqrt{2} x-8=0$. If $\\mathrm{U}_{\\mathrm{n}}=\\alpha^{\\mathrm{n}}+\\beta^n$, then $\\frac{\\mathrm{U}_{10}+\\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{U}_9}{2 \\mathrm{U}_8}$ is equal to______"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{\\alpha^{10}+\\beta^{10}+\\sqrt{2}\\left(\\alpha^9+\\beta^9\\right)}{2\\left(\\alpha^8+\\beta^8\\right)} \\\\ & \\frac{\\alpha^8\\left(\\alpha^2+\\sqrt{2} \\alpha\\right)+\\beta^8\\left(\\beta^2+\\sqrt{2} \\beta\\right)}{2\\left(\\alpha^8+\\beta^8\\right)} \\\\ & \\frac{8 \\alpha^8+8 \\beta^8}{2\\left(\\alpha^8+\\beta^8\\right)}=4\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}